!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = For neuroectoderm differentiation, neural progenitor cells were obtained using a previously established protocol for efficient neural differentiation with slight modification. To generate the NPCs, hESCs were plated on Matrigel-coated 6-well plates at a density of 2 million cells per well. The next day, mTeSR1 medium was replaced by embryoid body (EB) medium (knockout Dulbecco’s modified Eagle’s medium (DMEM) supplemented with 15% knockout serum replacement (KSR, Thermo Fisher Scientific), 2 mM L-glutamine, 0.1 mM nonessential amino acids, 50 units ml−1 penicillin, 50 µg ml−1 streptomycin and 0.1 mM β-mercaptoethanol) supplemented with 10 µM of SB431542 (Biogems) and 2.5 µM of LDN193189 (Biogems). EB medium (2 ml/well) was replaced every 24 hours for four days. Medium was then changed to a composite medium of EB medium and N-2 medium (Dulbecco’s Modified Eagle’s Medium/Nutrient Mixture F-12 Ham (Sigma), 1 x N-2 supplement (Thermo Fisher, cat. no. 17502001), 50 units ml−1 penicillin, 50 µg ml−1 streptomycin, 2 mM L-glutamine, 0.1 M ascorbic acid (Sigma) and 0.16 % D-Glucose) at a 3:1 ratio in the presence of 10 µM of SB431542 and 2.5 µM of LDN193189 for 24 hours.  The next day, medium was changed to a 1:1 ratio mix of EB medium and N-2 medium in the presence of 10 µM of SB431542 and 2.5 µM of LDN193189 for another 24 hours. The following day, the medium was changed to a 1:3 mix of EB medium and N-2 medium in the presence of 10 µM of SB431542 and 2.5 µM of LDN193189 for another 24 hours. Next, the medium was changed to N-2 medium in the presence of 10 µM of SB431542 and 2.5 µM of LDN193189 for another 24 hours and the cells were harvested the following day (9th day) for downstream analyses.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = hESCs were cultured at 37 0C and 5% CO2 in feeder-free conditions on Matrigel-coated plates (Corning) in mTeSR1 (STEMCELL Technologies).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = At the end of the differentiation assays, cells were harvested and total RNA was extracted with a RNeasy Mini Kit (QIAGEN).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = mRNA fraction of total RNA was enriched by pulldown of poly(A)-RNA. RNA sequencing libraries were generated using TruSeq RNA Library Prep Kit (Illumina) according to the manufacturer’s protocol and sequenced using Illumina NextSeq 500 with 75 bp single-end reads.
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were mapped to the reference genome and annotated using STAR 2.4.0.1 software.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: GRCh38 reference genome
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: comma separated values (csv) file contains transcript counts for each sample.
